    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="a5abcfd4-46ca-5a48-9509-1ce50b32993f" activityNameId="9a883716-d936-53cd-9ff6-8efaa45cbacd" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Trichloropropane, from hypochlorination of allyl chloride, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Trichloropropane, from hypochlorination of allyl chloride, at plant
Allyl chloride is reacted  with hylochlorous acid and calcium chloride to produce epichlorohydrin, calcium chloride and water;
UUID: 57d4cfbf-afc1-3904-88c5-01db000f0e6d
Multi-output process that produces 1 kg epichlorohydrin,  l.375 kg calcium chloride, and 18 kg of trichloropropane at plant. Economic allocation with allocation factor of 82.4% to epichlorohydrin, 16.2% to calcium chloride, and 1.4% to trichloropropane..
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: based on industry data in the US
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: literature data 
Extrapolations: Some data are derived from other or unknown plants or have been estimated.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_57d4cfbf-afc1-3904-88c5-01db000f0e6d.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="20a9bf48-6cea-59b4-ad08-000cb981f2d0" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
